WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.752
The Richmond Agitation-Sedation Scale is a structured observation scale developed for describing agitation and sedation. The AET module introduces it for prehospital assessment, but a score does not identify why the patient is agitated or less responsive.
Richmond躁动-镇静量表是一种结构化观察工具，用于描述躁动和镇静程度。AET模块将其引入院前评估，但分数不能说明患者躁动或反应降低的原因。

00:00:16.752 --> 00:00:29.640
Use this Week 10 supplement as shared vocabulary only when the course or current service protocol calls for it. Never let a scale delay immediate treatment of an airway, breathing or circulation threat.
只有课程或现行服务规程要求时，才把本补充内容作为共同语言。任何量表都不能延误对气道、呼吸或循环威胁的即时处理。

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:44.760
The scale ranges from plus four, combative, through zero, alert and calm, to minus five, unarousable. The negative anchors distinguish eye contact, voice response and response to physical stimulation.
量表从正四分的攻击性行为，经零分的清醒平静，到负五分的无法唤醒。负值锚点区分眼神接触、声音反应及对身体刺激的反应。

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:58.752
Follow the exact scoring method taught by your program and any current local protocol. This overview is not an independent bedside scoring credential or an instruction to apply physical stimulation outside training.
应遵循课程教授的准确评分方法及现行本地规程。本概述不是独立床旁评分资格，也不指示未经培训施加身体刺激。

00:00:58.752 --> 00:01:10.176
Zero means alert and calm. Plus one describes restlessness without aggressive or vigorous movement; it is not a score for every person who reports feeling anxious.
零分表示清醒平静。正一描述没有攻击性或剧烈动作的坐立不安，并非每位自述焦虑者都应得此分。

00:01:10.176 --> 00:01:25.080
Plus two describes frequent non-purposeful movement. The original ICU scale also includes fighting the ventilator. That example does not require an EMS patient to be ventilated before the behavioural anchor can be used.
正二描述频繁无目的动作。原始ICU量表也包括与呼吸机不同步的抗拒表现；这不要求EMS患者必须接受机械通气，才可使用该行为锚点。

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:39.888
Plus three includes pulling out a tube or catheter or aggressive behaviour. Plus four describes overt combative or violent conduct with immediate danger. Use the actual pattern, not how much the clinician dislikes the person’s words.
正三包括拔除管路或攻击性行为；正四描述明显对抗或暴力行为并造成即时危险。应依据实际模式，而非医护人员多不喜欢对方说的话。

00:01:39.888 --> 00:01:54.216
A score describes observed behaviour, not intent or a legal conclusion. Scene-safety decisions and medical assessment still require their own evidence; a positive score never creates automatic restraint permission.
分数描述观察到的行为，不是意图或法律结论。现场安全决定及医学评估仍需各自证据；正分从不自动授权约束。

00:01:54.216 --> 00:02:07.056
If the person is not alert, address them by name and ask them to open their eyes and look toward you. Observe whether they awaken and make eye contact; eye opening by itself is not the same finding.
患者不清醒时，呼叫姓名，请其睁眼并看向你。观察是否唤醒并建立眼神接触；单纯睁眼不是同一发现。

00:02:07.056 --> 00:02:22.104
Minus one is drowsiness with sustained awakening and eye contact to voice. Minus two is brief awakening with eye contact. The school and the SCCM chart contrast more than ten seconds with less than ten seconds.
负一是嗜睡，但对声音可持续唤醒并建立眼神接触；负二是短暂唤醒并建立眼神接触。学校与SCCM图表以超过10秒及少于10秒区分。

00:02:22.104 --> 00:02:40.008
The VCU web table uses ten seconds or more for minus one, while its introduction also contains an apparent plus-five range typo contradicted by its own table. Use the adopted chart and preserve the difference instead of inventing a universal boundary or a plus-five score.
VCU网页表格把10秒或以上列为负一；其介绍还有一个明显正五范围笔误，与其自身表格冲突。应使用采用版本并保留差异，不能自行创造通用边界或正五分。

00:02:40.008 --> 00:02:56.424
In rehearsal, use clear examples: six seconds of eye contact after the prompt fits minus two; fourteen seconds fits minus one under both wordings. At a boundary, record the observed duration and apply the complete local version.
演练可用明确例子：提示后眼神接触6秒符合负二，14秒在两种文字下都符合负一。遇到边界时，应记录实际时长并应用完整本地版本。

00:02:56.424 --> 00:03:09.600
A movement or eye opening caused by the verbal prompt, without eye contact, fits minus three. Do not call that no response merely because the person does not speak or obey a complex instruction.
声音提示引出的动作或睁眼，但没有眼神接触，符合负三。不能仅因患者没有说话或不遵从复杂指令，就称为无反应。

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:24.480
If there is no voice response, the approved physical step distinguishes minus four from minus five. A response in that step supports minus four; no response to either voice or the properly performed physical assessment supports minus five.
若对声音无反应，获准的身体刺激步骤用于区分负四与负五。该步骤有反应支持负四；声音及适当实施的身体评估均无反应，才支持负五。

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:41.664
The exact stimulus must follow current training and the patient context. The school mentions shoulder, jaw and orbital methods; the historical SCCM method and Northern Health palliative adaptation differ. Do not combine these into a new painful routine.
具体刺激须遵循现行训练及患者情境。学校提到肩部、下颌及眶部方法；历史SCCM方法与Northern Health姑息照护改编不同。不能把它们拼成一套新的疼痛刺激常规。

00:03:41.664 --> 00:04:00.048
Northern Health explicitly advises against sternal rubbing in palliative assessment. If stimulation is unsafe, inappropriate or not performed, document the limit and obtain assessment rather than manufacturing a complete score. Immediate life-threat care must not wait for scale completion.
Northern Health明确不建议在姑息评估中摩擦胸骨。若刺激不安全、不适当或未实施，应记录局限并取得评估，不能编出完整分数。即时生命威胁的照护不能等量表完成。

00:04:00.048 --> 00:04:13.656
A reproducible method makes comparisons more useful. Record the time, what prompt was used, what the patient did and what else was happening, such as pain, hypoxia concern, a recent medication or a seizure.
可重复的方法有助比较。应记录时间、使用的提示、患者反应及相关背景，例如疼痛、缺氧担忧、近期用药或发作。

00:04:13.656 --> 00:04:24.192
Do not score from a label such as “sleepy” or “aggressive” alone. Describe the actual response and document whether the patient’s state changed after an intervention.
不要只凭“困倦”或“攻击性”等标签评分。应描述实际反应，并记录干预后状态是否变化。

00:04:24.192 --> 00:04:36.336
Begin with spontaneous observation. If an alert and calm or positive agitation anchor is established, no additional stimulation is needed merely to finish three steps.
先观察自发状态。若已确定清醒平静或正值躁动锚点，就不需要仅为完成三步而再加刺激。

00:04:36.336 --> 00:04:51.840
For a person who is not alert, use the verbal assessment and observe awakening, eye contact and its duration. A voice response can establish minus one, minus two or minus three without proceeding to a physical stimulus.
对不清醒者使用声音评估，观察唤醒、眼神接触及时长。声音反应可确定负一、负二或负三，不需再进入身体刺激。

00:04:51.840 --> 00:05:03.312
Only absent voice response takes the scoring sequence toward the approved physical step. Follow the taught method and stop if the clinical context requires a different urgent response.
只有声音无反应，评分流程才继续考虑获准身体刺激。应遵循所教方法；若临床情境要求其他紧急回应，应停止量表流程。

00:05:03.312 --> 00:05:17.760
Record the score together with the method and time. A short sequence improves consistency only when its branches are respected; applying every stimulus to every patient is neither necessary nor faithful to the tool.
应把分数、方法及时间一起记录。简短流程只有遵守分支才能提高一致性；对每位患者施加全部刺激，既不必要，也不忠于工具。

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:35.040
A person may have a low score because of fatigue, medication, hypoxia, head injury, seizure, low glucose or another cause. A high score may reflect pain, fear, delirium, intoxication, hypoxia or a threat response.
低分可能来自疲劳、药物、缺氧、头伤、发作、低血糖或其他原因。高分可能来自疼痛、恐惧、谵妄、中毒、缺氧或对威胁的反应。

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:49.176
The scale cannot determine whether a person has decision-making capacity, whether a refusal is valid, or whether a restraint is permitted. Those questions require the relevant law, current pathway and full assessment.
量表不能决定患者是否有决定能力、拒绝是否有效，或约束是否被允许；这些问题需要适用法律、现行流程及完整评估。

00:05:49.176 --> 00:06:02.688
Before interpreting absent voice response, consider whether the prompt was accessible. Hearing loss, language mismatch or severe environmental noise can prevent the expected response without proving deeper sedation.
解释声音无反应前，应考虑提示是否可被接收。听力下降、语言不匹配或严重环境噪声，可能妨碍预期反应，却不证明镇静更深。

00:06:02.688 --> 00:06:17.400
Eye injury or visual impairment can limit the eye-contact observation. Movement limitation or paralysis can make a motor response unavailable. Do not turn an unobservable response into a negative finding automatically.
眼伤或视力障碍可限制眼神接触观察；运动障碍或瘫痪可使动作反应无法获得。不能自动把无法观察的反应当成阴性发现。

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:30.240
Describe the prompt, what occurred and why interpretation is limited. Seek an appropriate alternative clinical assessment under the current pathway instead of inventing a replacement RASS formula.
应描述提示、实际发生什么，以及判读为何受限。按现行流程取得适当替代临床评估，不能编造替代RASS公式。

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:43.128
A neurological examination, delirium assessment, capacity decision and airway evaluation answer different questions. The score can contribute shared language, but it does not replace those assessments.
神经检查、谵妄评估、决定能力判断及气道评估回答不同问题。分数可提供共同语言，却不能替代这些评估。

00:06:43.128 --> 00:06:57.792
If a patient becomes difficult to arouse, assess for immediate life threats before discussing scale trends. Preserve access to the airway and chest, check breathing and perfusion, and use your current PCP pathway.
若患者变得难以唤醒，应先检查即时生命威胁，再讨论量表趋势。保持气道和胸部可接近，评估呼吸及灌注，并遵循现行PCP流程。

00:06:57.792 --> 00:07:07.896
Repeat measurements with the same method when possible, but do not wait for a second score if the patient is collapsing, hypoventilating or cannot protect the airway.
条件允许时用相同方法复测，但若患者正在倒下、通气不足或无法保护气道，不要等待第二次评分。

00:07:07.896 --> 00:07:22.056
A trend is useful only when linked to clinical context. Ask about new medication, dose changes, substances, recent illness, head impact, a witnessed seizure, severe pain and the patient’s baseline.
只有与临床背景联系，趋势才有用。要询问新用药、剂量改变、物质使用、近期疾病、头部撞击、目击发作、剧痛及患者基线。

00:07:22.056 --> 00:07:34.008
A behavioral label must not hide physical deterioration. Conversely, a medical assessment should not erase the patient’s fear, goals or right to be treated respectfully.
行为标签不能掩盖身体恶化；反过来，医学评估也不能抹去患者的恐惧、目标或获得尊重对待的权利。

00:07:34.008 --> 00:07:48.408
Compare the score with respiratory effort, voice, eye opening, orientation, temperature, perfusion and the overall examination. A score that improves while breathing worsens is not an improvement in the whole patient.
将分数与呼吸用力、发声、睁眼、定向力、体温、灌注及整体检查结合。若分数改善但呼吸变差，不能说患者整体改善。

00:07:48.408 --> 00:08:00.360
Use trends to communicate urgency and response, not to create false precision. If the patient has a new decline, report the time course and escalate according to the current service pathway.
用趋势传达紧急程度及反应，而不是制造虚假的精确性。患者出现新发下降时，应报告时间经过并依现行服务流程升级处置。

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:13.944
In an original assessment example, a person awakens to their name and makes eye contact for six seconds. The observed anchor is minus two; it is not minus three because eye contact did occur.
原创评估例子中，患者听到姓名后唤醒，眼神接触持续6秒。观察锚点为负二，不是负三，因为确实有眼神接触。

00:08:13.944 --> 00:08:27.624
Later, using the same accessible prompt, eye contact lasts fourteen seconds. That observation fits minus one. Report the measured change and context, not simply that the number is better.
之后使用同样可接收提示，眼神接触持续14秒，符合负一。应报告测得变化及背景，而不只说数字更好了。

00:08:27.624 --> 00:08:40.248
A different patient moves an arm to voice but never makes eye contact. That fits the minus-three response pattern if the assessment is interpretable. A spoken answer is not required for that anchor.
另一患者听到声音后移动手臂，却始终没有眼神接触。评估可判读时，这符合负三反应模式；该锚点不要求口头回答。

00:08:40.248 --> 00:08:54.816
Check physiology alongside every comparison. If breathing effort or perfusion is worsening, a more awake appearance does not establish overall recovery. Treat the clinical change according to the current service pathway.
每次比较都应同时检查生理状态。若呼吸用力或灌注恶化，更清醒的外观不证明整体恢复。应按现行机构流程处理临床变化。

00:08:54.816 --> 00:09:10.584
Sedating medication can change respiratory drive, airway protection, blood pressure and responsiveness. Effects may combine with illness, alcohol or other substances, so deterioration must be actively sought.
镇静药物可改变呼吸驱动、气道保护、血压及反应性。药物作用可能与疾病、酒精或其他物质叠加，因此必须主动寻找恶化迹象。

00:09:10.584 --> 00:09:25.728
This course does not give medication doses or authorize PCP chemical restraint. Administer, assist with or monitor medication only as permitted by your licence, training, current service protocol and instructor direction.
本课程不提供药物剂量，也不授权PCP实施药物约束。只有在执照、培训、现行服务规程及教师指导允许时，才可给药、协助给药或监测。

00:09:25.728 --> 00:09:38.256
A good report avoids “RASS is minus three” as the only information. Add the actual stimulus and response, vital-sign trend, relevant history and the action taken.
良好报告不能只说“RASS负三”。还应补充实际刺激与反应、生命体征趋势、相关病史及已采取行动。

00:09:38.256 --> 00:09:49.032
Say what remains uncertain and what should be watched next. Keep the handover focused on patient safety, not on defending a label or a previous decision.
说明仍有哪些不确定，以及下一步需观察什么。交接应聚焦患者安全，而不是为标签或既往决定辩护。

00:09:49.032 --> 00:10:02.880
An original report could begin: At this assessment the patient opened their eyes to their name and held eye contact for six seconds, matching minus two on the chart in use. This is more informative than sleepy.
原创报告可这样开始：“本次评估中，患者听到姓名后睁眼，眼神接触6秒，符合使用图表的负二。”这比只说困倦更有信息。

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:16.008
Continue with the clinical findings you actually assessed and their trend. Add relevant medication or exposure history if known; do not imply that a negative RASS proves the person received a sedative.
继续报告真正检查过的临床发现及趋势。已知时补充相关用药或暴露史；不能暗示RASS负值就证明患者用过镇静药。

00:10:16.008 --> 00:10:27.840
State the action and response, including any inability to complete a component. Do not chart normal breathing, capacity or a physical-stimulus response that was not evaluated.
说明行动及反应，包括无法完成的部分。没有评估，就不能记录呼吸正常、具备决定能力，或对身体刺激的反应。

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:38.592
Finish with what remains concerning and who receives responsibility for follow-up. A complete sentence about the person is safer than handing over only a signed number.
最后说明仍有哪些担忧，以及由谁接手后续责任。关于患者的完整表述，比只交接一个带正负号的数字更安全。
